{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778941420,"nonce":"MXT0U+bh6XSI0frao9YrY0imOIY=","title":"Ledger UI: issue detail, comments, sync/conflict UX","message":"## Parent\nUmbrella: 097d2b7 — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nDepends on:\n- ff6a2bc — Ledger core.\n- aac782a — git-bug adapter/conflicts.\n- 59d527a — issue API cutover gates.\n- b45f19b — graph projection contracts for compact detail use.\n\n## Scope\nBuild the user-facing issue/work ledger surfaces needed to make the canonical backend usable and inspectable.\n\nThis issue owns:\n- ledger-backed issue detail component;\n- Markdown body rendering for issue descriptions;\n- comment timeline with actor/source badges;\n- add-comment flow writing through ledger commands;\n- labels/status/resolution/priority/kind display and safe mutation controls where implemented;\n- relationship display/edit affordances where backend support exists;\n- linked work-unit state and branch/worktree state;\n- linked sessions: active/idle first, historical collapsed;\n- linked auth requests/resolution shelf;\n- sync status, import/export job status, and conflict warnings;\n- conflict resolution UI actions: keep Mandible, accept external, manually merge;\n- compact graph-detail mode sharing the same issue detail primitives.\n\n## UX constraints\nThe UI should make operational state clear without turning every relationship into graph clutter.\n\nAuth requests usually appear as issue-attached evidence in issue mode. Dead sessions are history, not live graph actors. Sync/conflict state should be visible but not dominate normal issue reading unless action is required.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Implementing conflict detection internals.\n- Replacing every Issues tab workflow at once if route compatibility is still gated.\n- Building a generic external-tracker UI.\n\n## Verification\n- Component tests for issue detail rendering, comments, badges, and empty states.\n- API integration tests for add-comment/status/label flows where implemented.\n- Browser smoke for issue list/detail, graph detail compact mode, add comment, sync status, and conflict surface.\n- Accessibility/keyboard checks for conflict actions and comment form.\n- Build verification: `npm run build`.\n\n## Done means\nA user can inspect the canonical issue content, comments, relationships, auth evidence, session/work history, and sync/conflict state without needing to drop to git-bug or interpret raw ledger records.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}